  "reflectionText": "John stood in the wilderness in camel's hair with a leather belt around his waist, ate locusts and wild honey, and cried out: repent. He pointed to the One coming after him whose sandals he was not worthy to carry. What is the courage of standing in the desert as the voice of one crying out, when all the people you call must come out of their cities to hear you?"
